 ## Overview
-Gaussian Interpolation uses a Gaussian function as an interpolation kernel to reconstruct signals from discrete samples. It is distinguished from other filters by being the only filter that is both separable and rotationally symmetric [S1, unofficial]. This unique property allows it to integrate one dimension out of the kernel, enabling 2D reconstruction instead of 3D, which is particularly advantageous in point-tossing approaches like splatting [S1, unofficial].
