 **Pitfalls and Edge Cases:**
 - **Infinite Extent:** The Gaussian kernel has infinite extent in both spatial and frequency domains [S1, unofficial]. In practice, it must be truncated. Because it asymptotically falls to zero quickly, truncation can be performed in the near-zero area without causing significant ringing artifacts [S1, unofficial].
-- **Blurring:** The filter distorts the passband by attenuating high-frequency components of the main replica, which causes blurring in the output [S1, unofficial]. This makes it less suitable for applications requiring sharp edge preservation compared to filters with sharper cutoffs.
