 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** $O(N)$ where $N$ is the number of samples within the truncation radius. Due to separability, an $N$-dimensional interpolation can be decomposed into $N$ one-dimensional interpolations, reducing computational cost [S1, unofficial].
-- **Memory Complexity:** Low, as the kernel is defined by a single parameter $\sigma$ and does not require large lookup tables [S1, unofficial].
