 ## Background
-Gaussian interpolation has been used in various research contexts for signal reconstruction. It is notably used in point-tossing approaches like splatting [Westover 90] because of its separability and rotational symmetry, which allow for efficient 2D reconstruction [S1, unofficial]. In the context of volumetric rendering, it has been applied in temporal anti-aliasing methods for froxel-based rendering to improve edge quality and stability [S2, unofficial]. The specific Gaussian fit to Blackman-Harris 3.3 was introduced by Karis for use in TAA [S2, unofficial].
